  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/heritagegraph/FearlessnessAssessment">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>FearlessnessAssessment</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/heritagegraph/RitualAssessment"/>
    <skos:definition>The 'fearlessness test' popularly described (animal heads, masked dancers in darkness). Its historical and contemporary practice is DISPUTED -- some former Kumaris contest how it is described. Represented as an assessment whose accounts are source-attributed via has_assertion, NOT as a mandatory criterion.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/heritagegraph/schema"/>
    <skos:scopeNote>Deliberately not a SelectionCriterion subclass: popular accounts and lived testimony disagree. Attach each account as a Assertion (CRMinf I2 Belief) with its own source and confidence.</skos:scopeNote>
  </rdf:Description>
